{"term":"awake","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1522103ef2e07d81a5","definition":"Not asleep; conscious.","example":"By quarter to six all this had me so awake and agitated that even the Balinese wind chimes that I hung up in the garden to relax me began to sound like Big Ben.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["conscious","lucid","wide awake"],"antonyms":["asleep","unconscious","asleep","cold","comatose","dead to the world","dormant","down for the count","in the arms of Morpheus","in the arms of Murphy","nangry","out cold","out like a light","sacked out","sleepbound","sleeping","somnambular","unawakening","unawaking","unwaking"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, predicative","register":"not-comparable, predicative","wordFamily":["awakeness","be awake","broad awake","half-awake","nonawake","unawake","wide-awake","wideawake"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:989adf6ec7c40aaef3","definition":"Alert, aware.","example":"They were awake to the possibility of a decline in sales.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["wary","woke","alert","aware","heedful","hip","observant","on guard","on the lookout","on the watch","on watch","vigilant","wakeful","wakesome","wary","watchful","woke"],"antonyms":["heedless","oblivious"],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, figuratively, predicative","register":"broadly, figuratively, predicative","wordFamily":["awakeness","be awake","broad awake","half-awake","nonawake","unawake","wide-awake","wideawake"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:307153738882b9a68c","definition":"To become conscious after having slept.","example":"Awake! for Morning in the Bowl of Night,\nHas flung the Stone that puts the Stars to Flight:\nAnd Lo! the Hunter of the East has ca